  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cyclone Idai and Kenneth Emergency Recovery and Resilience Project -CERRP (P171040)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">much evidence that the cyclone-affected populations have been very dynamic in re-starting their own livelihoods, and to the degree possible, in initiating repair or reconstruction of their own housing. However, there are many households who have not had the resources to start the recovery process, and who remain in very vulnerable houses. With a severe drop-off of capacities amongst humanitarian actors and limited response of development actors with shelter and housing capacities, but also a recurrence of the cyclone alerts, the Government of Mozambique is looking to initiate a larger-scale programme of construction of complete permanent core houses and resilient repairs.Over the last 3 years, IOM has led a reconstruction program that supported cyclone-affected communities with resilient and permanent houses across northern and central Mozambique. Building on that experience and grounded in human rights principles and utilization of innovative processes that build social cohesion and support community ownership, IOM is emphasising the integration of Build Back Safer materials and improved techniques to deliver the construction and retrofits of 3,240 resilient housing solutions.</narrative>
  </description>
